    "case_id": "660",
    "case_summary": "A 71-year-old patient with recurrent stage IIIC papillary serous adenocarcinoma of the ovary. Initial treatment included resection and 6 cycles of adjuvant paclitaxel/carboplatin. One year later, the patient developed liver and cecal metastases. Over the next seven years, the patient underwent multiple treatments and developed metastases to the right pleura, abdominal masses, and new liver and splenic metastases. The patient was negative for germline mutation but positive for somatic mutation.\n\nNo specific physical examination findings were detailed in the case report.\n\n{'Laboratory Tests': '- CA125 levels increased from 145.6 to 271.7', 'Imaging Studies': '- CT scans showed:      - Progressive disease with hepatic and splenic lesions      - Metastases to right pleura      - Two abdominal masses      - Liver and splenic metastases', 'Molecular Testing': '- Foundation One sequencing of metastatic tumor tissue    - Three serial ctDNA analyses (Guardant360) showing:      First collection: BRCA-1 mutation (c. 2563C > T p. Q855*) at 33.3% MAF      Second collection: BRCA-1 mutation increased to 50.7% MAF      Third collection: BRCA-1 mutation decreased to 27.2% MAF'}",
